As seen in the 'Number of Players Accounted For' column, the total_estimated_cost is accounting for 7 to 8 players when FD has 9 players per lineup. Despite giving some wiggle room with the .9 multiplier in the calculation below, I believe the calculation is still too low. https://github.com/chanzer0/MLB-DFS-Tools/blob/0be2275e6d9feeecccc6131dfccd2fda9114fdcc/src/mlb_gpp_simulator.py#L1205

## Suggested Edits
I suggest replacing the code on lines [1188-1206](https://github.com/chanzer0/MLB-DFS-Tools/blob/0be2275e6d9feeecccc6131dfccd2fda9114fdcc/src/mlb_gpp_simulator.py#L1188-L1206) with the below code. The changes include altering the calculation for `max_secondary_stack_len`, adding a variable `num_extra_hitters`, and replacing the if/else statement for a more dynamic calculation of `total_estimated_cost`

```python

if primary_teams[-1] and np.random.rand() < self.pct_field_using_secondary_stacks:
    #use primary_stack_len to set secondary_stack_len
    max_secondary_stack_len = min((num_hitters_per_lineup - primary_lens[-1]), self.max_stack_len)
    available_teams = [team for team in teams if team != primary_teams[-1]]
    secondary_stack_len = np.random.choice([max_secondary_stack_len-1,max_secondary_stack_len], p=[0.5,0.5])
    filtered_teams = []
    num_extra_hitters = len(self.roster_construction) - (primary_lens[-1] + secondary_stack_len + num_pitchers)
    for team in available_teams:
        # Check financial feasibility
        total_estimated_cost = (team_average_salaries[primary_teams[-1]] * primary_lens[-1] + # Primary Stack Avg Sal
                                team_average_salaries[team] * secondary_stack_len + # Secondary Stack Avg Sal 
                                average_hitter_salary * num_extra_hitters + # Avg Sal for all hitters not in stacks
                                average_pitcher_salary * num_pitchers)  # Avg Pitcher Sal                       
        if self.min_lineup_salary *.9 <= total_estimated_cost <= self.salary:
            filtered_teams.append(team)
```
